{
  "schema": 1,
  "what": "R0's preflight: the situations the runner under qualification is put in and what is checked afterwards. The runner is the one R0 names, run through its adapter; the states are synthetic and built fresh for each situation. preflight.schema.json beside this file states the shapes and what each check decides.",
  "interface": {
    "evaluator": "The dated evaluator the current plan names in `validator`, beside the plan, run as `python3 <evaluator> <plan> --run <run.json>`: exit 0 when the terminal claims hold, 2 when not yet, 1 when the run is invalid. Its JSON body's `eligible[mode]` lists the nodes that may be dispatched in that mode and `rejected_nodes[node]` the reasons a node is not accepted; its `digest` is the canonical digest every identity in a packet uses. `gates/check-development-plan.py` is not this evaluator: that gate accepts only `--self-test`.",
    "invocation": "invocation.schema.json",
    "packet": "packet.schema.json",
    "worker_result": "worker-result.schema.json",
    "report": "report.schema.json"
  },
  "construction": {
    "run": "The driver loads the current plan, its catalog, the dated evaluator (`validator`) and the regression suite (`regression_tests`) beside it; builds the suite's `Fixture(evaluator, plan, catalog, <situation directory>, unattended=<base is unattended>)`; applies the situation's changes in order to the Fixture's run; and writes that run as `run.json` in the Fixture's artifact directory, so record artifacts resolve beside it. Every record carries the suite's marker SYNTHETIC-AUTHOR-REGRESSION-NOT-PRODUCT-EVIDENCE. The run's `runner_fingerprint` is the Fixture's own; the adapter under qualification is what R0's real record will bind, not this synthetic value.",
    "tree": "A new git repository `tree` in the situation directory, with one commit holding revision 1 of every listed file and, when any file has two revisions, a second commit adding revision 2 of those. An empty file list still makes one commit, of an empty `.keep` file. HEAD after these commits is the base every packet must name.",
    "stubs": "The invocation's `worker_command` runs the driver's stub worker with the packet path. For each packet the stub appends a start line and, on finishing, an end line to the driver's stub log, each naming the node id, the attempt id and the sha256 of the packet bytes; writes one evidence file `stub-evidence.txt` in the packet's `evidence_dir` holding `SYNTHETIC-RUNNER-EVIDENCE <node_id> <attempt_id>` and a newline; and writes its worker_result at the packet's `result_path`: the stub row's outcome, one change per append with `base_digest` the sha256 of the bytes it read, and the evidence file.",
    "restart": "After a stopped round the driver leaves the situation directory exactly as the round left it (run file, tree, results, evidence, stub log) and runs the same invocation without `stop_at`. `always` applies to every round that was not stopped; a situation's checks read the state after its last round."
  },
  "always": [
    "report_conforms",
    "packets_conform",
    "evaluated_as_the_plan_evaluates",
    "dispatches_equal_eligible",
    "within_concurrency_ceiling",
    "report_matches_stub_log",
    "reconciliations_cover_in_flight",
    "applied_rows_match_the_tree",
    "terminal_claim_matches_evaluator"
  ],
